  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v.1.5.0\n- Update: Added support for .NET 11\n- Feature: Added the DrainTimeoutWhenDisposing option. Dispose() now waits for the rest of the output for up to 5 seconds by default, so it no longer hangs when a child process keeps the output open.\n- Improve: Output async streams started after the process exited now return the lines not yet read, instead of nothing.\n- Improve: WaitForOutputAsync() no longer clears the buffered output, so the Output, StdOutput, and StdError properties keep all lines after the call.\n- Fix: Resolved an issue where the Output, StdOutput, and StdError properties could be incomplete right after WaitForExitAsync() completed (Issue #1).\n- Fix: Resolved an issue where output async streams could miss the last lines of a process.\n- Fix: Resolved an issue where WaitForOutputAsync() could return true at once, matching a line that an earlier WaitForOutputAsync() call had already checked.\n- Fix: Resolved an issue where the ExitCode property became 0 after Dispose() even when the process had not exited. It is now null in that case.\n\n\nTo see all the change logs, please visit the following URL.\n- https://github.com/jsakamoto/XProcess/blob/master/RELEASE-NOTES.txt",
